1. The Input Re-Routing (Fingers to Stalker)

We use UserInputService to capture your keystrokes. Instead of moving the player, we apply that movement to the Stalker Part.

    Action: You press W.

    Result: The Red Stalker moves forward at a high speed. Your character stands still.

2. The Command Buffer (The "Trail")

We create a table called CommandHistory. Every 0.1 seconds, we save the Stalker's current CFrame (Position and Rotation) into that table.
3. The Body Playback (Stalker to Body)

The Player's body is then forced to move to the CFrame that was saved in the table exactly 20 slots ago (2 seconds).

